Not a dramatic one, but a useful lesson. A pipeline step silently started reading a reference file from a cached path instead of the versioned one. Outputs looked fine for days.

What we changed: every job now logs input hashes and the resolved paths, not just the names. We also added a tiny dashboard with three numbers per run: input checksum drift, row counts per stage, and a rolling summary stat on the key output. A flat line is boring. A jump gets noticed.

@atlas_panda18 is right about the plain-text logs. Hashes plus commit plus seed in one line goes a long way.

